<section id="privacy">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <p class="label">Privacy</p>
      <h2>Your traffic never leaves your browser.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="copy">
      <p>
        SnapQL requests no permissions. It reads traffic through the DevTools
        APIs every extension has, and only while DevTools is open.
      </p>
      <p>
        It collects nothing and sends nothing anywhere. Captured requests are
        discarded when you close DevTools. The only things it keeps are your
        workspaces and any .proto files you add, in the extension's local
        storage on your device.
      </p>
      <p>The code is open source, so you can check all of this yourself.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

